docs {
  # Get Validate Request By Created By

  This request is used to validate a user's token. It is not implemented in the business logic, but serves only for end-to-end (E2E) and integration testing. It provides an alternative way to obtain a token if another request has already sent the token via email or Telegram. This request interacts with the MySQL database and is protected by route authentication.

  ## Path Parameters

  | Name       | Type   | Required | Description                          |
  |------------|--------|----------|----------------------------------------|
  | type       | string | yes      | Request type (e.g. `register`)       |
  | created_by | string | yes      | ID of the user who created the request |

  ## Responses

  **200 — User request fetched successfully**
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "user request",
    "data": "ABC123"
  }
```

  **401 — protected route need to include api key**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the api key"
  }
```

  **404 — user request failed to fetched**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "user request not found"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}